<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · Mesopotamia and Iran</p><h1 class="st-title">Second Sealand Dynasty</h1><p class="st-meta">1025 BCE – 1005 BCE (approx.) · capital Babylon</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A brief Babylonian dynasty of three kings around 1000 BCE, founded by Simbar-Shipak in a time of Aramean raids and famine.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/simbar-shipak">Simbar-Shipak</a>, who claimed descent from the southern marshlands, took the throne of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/babylon">Babylon</a> in 1025 BCE after the end of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/second-dynasty-of-isin">Second Dynasty of Isin</a>. Babylonian king lists call his line the dynasty of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/sealand-dynasty">Sealand</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The dynasty ruled a weakened <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/babylonia">Babylonia</a> troubled by Aramean and Sutean incursions. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/simbar-shipak">Simbar-Shipak</a> restored the throne of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/enlil">Enlil</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ekur">Ekur</a> at <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/nippur">Nippur</a>, damaged by raiders, and is mentioned in later chronicles. He was murdered after eighteen years; his successor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ea-mukin-zeri">Ea-mukin-zeri</a> reigned only months, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kashshu-nadin-ahi">Kashshu-nadin-ahi</a> ruled for three years amid shortages that halted temple offerings.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>The dynasty ended around 1005 BCE and was replaced by the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/bazi-dynasty">Bazi Dynasty</a>.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/second-sealand-dynasty.jpg" alt="Second Sealand Dynasty" width="320" height="391"><figcaption>Image: Wikimedia Commons · CC BY 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Harran_Stela.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1025 BCE – 1005 BCE (approx.)</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/11th-century-bce">11th century BCE</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>bureaucratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Babylon</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Simbar-Shipak, Ea-mukin-zeri, Kashshu-nadin-ahi</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Babylonian religion</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Akkadian</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/iraq">Iraq</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Fifth Dynasty of Babylon</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=-1015&amp;focus=second-sealand-dynasty" aria-label="Second Sealand Dynasty on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5820 995 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Second Sealand Dynasty lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M6140 1251L6140 1251M6140 1251L6140 1251"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M6140 1251h0M6140 1251h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M6140 1251h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M6140 1251h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Babylon. <a href="/atlas?year=-1015&amp;focus=second-sealand-dynasty">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
